• Excluding the volatile tender-driven crop insurance and government health business, Bajaj General posted a GDPI growth rate of 11.8% in line with industry growth.
• Bajaj General continues to be among the most profitable general insurers in India. Its combined ratio (COR) of 102.8% in FY2026 is expected to be among the best in the industry, reflecting a sound balance between growth and profitability. Bajaj General has achieved this by:
(a) robust and prudent underwriting practices driven by strong analytics based on past claims experience;
(b) diversified exposure across business lines and geographies;
(c) granular loss ratio modelling;
(d) robust investigation and loss management;
(e) generation of cash flows through strong retention of premium and judicious investments of the proceeds; and
(f) focus on high quality customer service.
• Bajaj General has a diversified and among the largest multi-channel distribution network consisting of banks, NBFCs, individual agents, motor insurance service providers, point of salespersons, web-sales and its proprietary direct to customers’ channel. It continued to expand the network of bancassurance partners including private banks, public sector banks, regional banks, small finance banks and cooperative banks. Bajaj General has one of the largest networks of bancassurance partners in general insurance.

